#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama config generate
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:38
msgid ""
"Generate and print a native Agama JSON configuration from any kind and "
"location."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama config generate (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:40
msgid ""
"Kinds:\n"
"- JSON\n"
"- Jsonnet, injecting the hardware information\n"
"- AutoYaST profile, including ERB and rules/classes\n"
"\n"
"Locations:\n"
"- path\n"
"- URL (including AutoYaST specific schemes)\n"
"\n"
"For an example of Jsonnet-based profile, see\n"
"https://github.com/openSUSE/agama/blob/master/rust/agama-lib/share/examples/"
"profile.jsonnet"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama config edit
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:44
msgid "Edit and update installation option using an external editor"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama config edit (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:46
msgid ""
"The changes are not applied if the editor exits with an error code.\n"
"\n"
"If an editor is not specified, it honors the EDITOR environment variable. It "
"falls back to `/usr/bin/vi` as a last resort."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama config edit --editor <EDITOR>
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:48
msgid "Editor command (including additional arguments if needed)"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama probe
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:50
#, fuzzy
msgid "Analyze the system"
msgstr "Προετοιμασία του συστήματος"

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama probe (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:52
msgid ""
"In Agama's jargon, the term 'probing' refers to the process of 'analyzing' "
"the system. This includes reading software repositories, analyzing storage "
"devices, and more. The 'probe' command initiates this analysis process and "
"returns immediately. TODO: do we really need a \"probe\" action?"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama install
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:54
msgid "Start the system installation"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama install (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:56
msgid ""
"This command starts the installation process.  Beware it is a destructive "
"operation because it will set up the storage devices, install the packages, "
"etc.\n"
"\n"
"When the preconditions for the installation are not met, it informs the user "
"and returns, making no changes to the system."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:58
msgid "Handle installer questions"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:60
msgid ""
"Agama might require user intervention at any time. The reasons include "
"providing some missing information (e.g., the password to decrypt a file "
"system) or deciding what to do in case of an error (e.g., cannot connect to "
"the repository).\n"
"\n"
"This command allows answering such questions directly from the command-line."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions mode
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:62
msgid "Set the mode for answering questions"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions answers
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:64
msgid "Load predefined answers"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions answers (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:66
msgid ""
"It allows predefining answers for specific questions in order to skip them "
"in interactive mode or change the answer in automatic mode.\n"
"\n"
"Please check Agama documentation for more details and examples: https://"
"github.com/openSUSE/agama/blob/master/doc/questions."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions answers <PATH>
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:68
msgid "Path to a file containing the answers in JSON format"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions list
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:70
msgid ""
"Prints the list of questions that are waiting for an answer in JSON format"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama questions ask
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:72
msgid ""
"Reads a question definition in JSON from stdin and prints the response when "
"it is answered"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:74
msgid "Collect the installer logs"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:76
msgid ""
"The installer logs are stored in a compressed archive for further "
"inspection. The file includes system and Agama-specific logs and "
"configuration files. They are crucial to troubleshoot and debug problems."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs store
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:78
msgid "Collect and store the logs in a tar archive"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs store --destination <DESTINATION>
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:80
msgid ""
"Path to destination directory and, optionally, the archive file name. The "
"extension will be added automatically"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama logs list
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:82
msgid "List the logs to collect"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama auth
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:84
msgid "Authenticate with Agama's server"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama auth (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:86
msgid ""
"Unless you are executing this program as root, you need to authenticate with "
"Agama's server for most operations. You can log in by specifying the root "
"password through the \"auth login\" command. Upon successful authentication, "
"the server returns a JSON Web Token (JWT) which is stored to authenticate "
"the following requests.\n"
"\n"
"If you run this program as root, you can skip the authentication step "
"because it automatically uses the master token at /run/agama/token. Only the "
"root user must have access to such a file.\n"
"\n"
"You can logout at any time by using the \"auth logout\" command, although "
"this command does not affect the root user."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama auth login
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:88
msgid "Authenticate with Agama's server and store the token"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama auth login (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:90
msgid ""
"This command tries to get the password from the standard input. If it is not "
"there, it asks the user interactively. Upon successful login, it stores the "
"token in .agama/agama-jwt. The token will be automatically sent to "
"authenticate the following requests."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama auth logout
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:92
msgid "Deauthenticate by removing the token"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama auth show
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:94
msgid "Print the used token to the standard output"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama download
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:96
msgid "Download file from a given (AutoYaST) URL"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama download (details)
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:98
msgid ""
"The purpose of this command is to download files using AutoYaST supported "
"schemas (e.g. device://). It can be used to download additional scripts, "
"configuration files and so on. You can use it for downloading Agama "
"autoinstallation profiles. If you want to convert an AutoYaST profile, use "
"\"agama config generate\"."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: command: agama download <URL>
#: agama-cli/src/cli_strings.rs:100
